  "notes": "Both SKS workbooks were read via openpyxl (data_only=True), sheet \"Repayment Schedule\" (primary), cross-checked against \"Disbursement\", \"SKS Edible Oil_Loan\", and \"Summary\" sheets. Cell comments in the 2nd Restructure workbook (author annotations on the Summary sheet, e.g. \"Jan'21 Interest\", \"Jul'22 Principal (Partial)\") confirm this file was a live payment-tracking workbook updated through at least 2025, i.e. it reflects the loan's actual current/operative schedule.\n\nBoth restructure files are byte-identical in their first 31 rows (2018-06-15 through 2020-12-15, the original interest-accrual/capitalization stub matching the ORIGINAL EX_DATA['SKS'] trajectory), then diverge starting exactly at row 32 = 2021-01-14 (serial 44210), which I used as the shared effective date for both versions.\n\nVersion 1 (1st Restructure, Feb'21 file): opening balance 2,462,366,017.845 at 2021-01-14, rate cut from 10% to 8.25%, principal_type switched from \"Scheduled Principal\" to \"Annuity\", day-count basis unchanged at 360, 96 remaining installments (matches the workbook's stated \"Number of installments: 96\"), fully amortizes to 0 by 2028-12-15. Capitalized amount of ~228.6M BDT was computed as the difference between this version's opening balance and where the ORIGINAL (unrestructured, 10%) schedule's closing balance would have stood on 2020-12-15 (2,233,766,722.25) — i.e., extra unpaid interest from the extended interest-only/negotiation period that got folded into principal at restructuring.\n\nVersion 2 (2nd Restructure, Sep'21 file, classified as MORATORIUM_EXTENSION since rate/principal-type are unchanged from v1 and the only substantive change is a further extension of the interest-only period): same starting balance and rate as v1 (2,462,366,017.845 @ 8.25%), but the amortizing/principal-repayment phase that v1 had scheduled to start 2021-01-14 was pushed back — the workbook instead continued interest-only payments through 2022-06-15, with principal resuming 2022-07-14 at a flat annuity-style installment of ~25,678,862.61/month, extending final maturity to 2030-06-15 (114 total remaining installments instead of v1's 96, i.e. tenor extended by roughly 18 months net of the original schedule). There is a small secondary capitalization of ~2.8M BDT at 2021-07-15 (closing balance jumps from 2,462,366,017.845 to 2,465,170,810.937) which I've recorded as this version's capitalizedAmount. The workbook's own \"Number of installments\" header field still says 96 in both restructure files (apparently not updated for the 2nd restructure's longer schedule) — I used the actual row count (114) for num_installments in the params object since accuracy of the regenerable schedule was prioritized per instructions. The 2nd restructure's effectiveDate is set to the same 2021-01-14 as v1 (rather than the Sep'21 document/filename date) because the schedule rows show it retroactively supersedes v1's entire amortization plan from that same starting point rather than taking over mid-stream from v1's partially-paid balance — this is a judgment call; the Sep'21 filename most likely reflects when the restructuring was formally documented/approved, applied retroactively back to Jan'21.\n\nNo true waivers (forgiveness) were found in either file — all balance increases are capitalization of accrued/unpaid interest, not debt forgiveness, so waivedAmount = 0 for both versions. No explicit regulatory circular reference (e.g. \"DFIM Circular\") was found anywhere in either workbook's cells or comments, so regulatoryReference is null for both. Rate remained unchanged (8.25%) between the two restructure versions, and principal_type/day-count-basis/currency/lender were also unchanged — only the moratorium length, remaining installment count, and a small incremental capitalization differ.\n\nInterest_day_adjustments, principal_schedule_percentages, and interest_rates_by_period were left null for both versions (not present in the workbook data and not needed since override arrays pin every row exactly, matching the pattern used for MCML/QPSL/SCBL/SKS/THERMAX in the ORIGINAL examples.ts fixtures). The \"interest_rate_change_events\" array is included as a single entry at the effective date for documentation purposes even though the override arrays make it non-authoritative for regeneration."
